                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dd870816-8961-38b0-b45c-de192a4742a9",
                        "entry_id": "6191c6e5-6321-33f0-991d-3fcfaf6a3ddd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die te veel kletst, plaats waar teveel gekletst wordt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcfa44c3-efb0-4125-956a-3a0e6b26b421",
                                "sense_id": "dd870816-8961-38b0-b45c-de192a4742a9",
                                "text": "Ondanks alle verhalen en verbaasde blikken, van productiemeisjes die elkaar onopvallend met hun ellebogen aantikten, hield Ineke haar hoofd recht. ,,Ze houdt gewoon van die man’’, zegt een ingewijde, die zelf echter ook twijfelt of ze Humberto opnieuw de openlijke vernedering kan vergeven die haar eerder ten deel viel. Maar dit weekend steunde ze hem, in het hol van de leeuw: in het praatzieke Hilversum."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9c4d8c8-3dff-4b2c-b25f-103798810d74",
                                "sense_id": "dd870816-8961-38b0-b45c-de192a4742a9",
                                "text": "Ook Stephen Fry, die de uitreiking van de Bafta’s presenteerde, bleek geen vriend van Trump. De acteur, komiek, schrijver en presentator steunde Meryl Streep, die bij de uitreiking van de Golden Globes uithaalde naar de Amerikaanse president. “Ze is een van de beste actrices ooit. Alleen een praatzieke idioot zou daar anders over denken.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "71a65d2e-8b9f-439c-b453-32567162513b",
                        "source_entry_id": "6191c6e5-6321-33f0-991d-3fcfaf6a3ddd",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd870816-8961-38b0-b45c-de192a4742a9",
                        "target_lang_word": "loquacious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loquacious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffa6b84f-160c-354f-90fb-f31a0a2f8ec7",
                                        "entry_id": "433f714d-c63b-36fe-9fdc-bfb8c48a0560",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Talkative; chatty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05a821ce-0376-420f-b868-67b96f7543b5",
                                                "sense_id": "ffa6b84f-160c-354f-90fb-f31a0a2f8ec7",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, Hetty was moody and silent. She was never loquacious, or if she occasionally became communicative, it was under the influence of some temporary excitement that served to arouse her unsophisticated mind; but, for hours at a time, in the course of this all-important day, she seemed to have absolutely lost the use of her tongue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8032f062-fee2-4d37-a3ba-c58b425b99e1",
                                                "sense_id": "ffa6b84f-160c-354f-90fb-f31a0a2f8ec7",
                                                "text": "\"[…]and as Mr. H., with his long purse and his willingness to receive hints, is no bad card in the game, he has been brought up to Abbotsford for a week; his taciturnity has long ago fled, and he is one of the most loquacious Borderers going. […]\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5497beeb-8091-4ce8-b283-4c4767156645",
                        "source_entry_id": "6191c6e5-6321-33f0-991d-3fcfaf6a3ddd",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd870816-8961-38b0-b45c-de192a4742a9",
                        "target_lang_word": "garrulous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "garrulous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38e81b67-1b81-36b8-a4f5-2e49314d5879",
                                        "entry_id": "d4c451e4-ae8c-3468-9dd6-0dbc77ddf86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessively or tiresomely talkative."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "316875c7-97a8-4ee6-a546-6e964ae43d84",
                                                "sense_id": "38e81b67-1b81-36b8-a4f5-2e49314d5879",
                                                "text": "She lingered for a few moments, and was garrulous over some detail of the household."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b491fd27-b9ad-41bb-a333-2eb00755bd31",
                                                "sense_id": "38e81b67-1b81-36b8-a4f5-2e49314d5879",
                                                "text": "Crammed with gossip, anecdotes, and confessions . . ., his garrulous, untidy narratives read like a good novel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "021047d7-9329-3a30-ad87-cafb810c9405",
                                        "entry_id": "d4c451e4-ae8c-3468-9dd6-0dbc77ddf86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessively wordy and rambling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of something written or performed"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4025fa56-bcee-4b88-8b5c-6acb3a20870a",
                        "source_entry_id": "6191c6e5-6321-33f0-991d-3fcfaf6a3ddd",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd870816-8961-38b0-b45c-de192a4742a9",
                        "target_lang_word": "talkative",
